  {
    "start": 67.89999999999999,
    "end": 103.425,
    "narration": "For the next two decades he grew it the way most shipping fortunes get built: patiently, and through acquisition. In 1996 he bought Compagnie G\u00e9n\u00e9rale Maritime \u2014 the former state-owned French line that once ran legendary transatlantic liners like the Normandie, a fading piece of national pride, privatized and struggling. He turned it profitable within a year, merged it with his own company in 1999, and instantly had the twelfth-largest shipping line on Earth. By 2006, it was already third.",
