  {
    "start": 103.425,
    "end": 135.275,
    "narration": "Then the acquisitions stopped being about ships at all. In 2016, CMA CGM spent 2.4 billion dollars buying Singapore's Neptune Orient Lines. Three years later it bought CEVA Logistics, a freight-forwarding company operating in over 160 countries \u2014 and that deal changed what the company actually was. It didn't just want to move your container across an ocean anymore. It wanted to own every step before and after, too.",
