  {
    "start": 193.17499999999998,
    "end": 239.825,
    "narration": "And that kind of freedom is exactly how a shipping company ends up owning a news channel. In 2024, Rodolphe Saad\u00e9 spent 1.55 billion euros on BFM-TV, France's most-watched news channel, plus the radio station RMC, two newspapers, and a stake in the broadcaster M6. None of it has anything to do with containers. What it did was put Saad\u00e9 in direct competition for French public opinion with Vincent Bollor\u00e9, another industrial tycoon who owns the rival channel CNews. Two logistics billionaires, fighting over French television \u2014 because when a company answers to no one but its own family, there's nothing stopping it from becoming one.",
